course: dictionary
lesson: 6681
title: Noticing and watching
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An observation is what you notice when you watch something carefully. Observation is the act of watching closely. Scientists make observations, writing down what they see, hear and feel during an experiment.
explain: Read the example: «natural grace which goes with perfect unconsciousness of observation». The people look natural because they do not know anyone is watching them. The clue is unconsciousness, which means not being aware of something, so observation must mean being watched.
explain: Observation can also mean being checked closely. A patient may be kept under observation, which means doctors watch them carefully. Ask yourself: what is being watched, and why? That question will help you find the meaning.
fact: Observation means watching something carefully to learn about it.
fact: An observation is something you noticed or recorded, often in science.
fact: An observation can also be a remark or comment about something you noticed.
fact: «Under observation» means being watched carefully, for example by doctors.
fact: In science lessons, pupils record observations in tables, notes and drawings.
exercise: «natural grace which goes with perfect unconsciousness of observation» What does observation mean here? | Being lost | Being cold | *Being watched | Being hungry
exercise: In science, Mia writes down what she sees in a table. What is each thing she writes called? | Mistakes | Holidays | Puddles | *Observations
exercise: A nurse says, «He is under observation tonight.» What does under observation mean? | Being very hungry | *Being watched carefully | Being asleep in bed | Being sent home
test: Which phrase means someone is being watched carefully by doctors? | A loud remark | *Under observation | A happy mood | A science table
test: Which word fits best? «She wrote down her ___ in the notebook after the experiment.» | Holidays | *Observations | Mistakes | Dinner
exam: What does powers of observation mean? | *The skill of watching and noticing things carefully | Sleeping very well at night | Talking loudly in class | Being careless about small things
